---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import FeatureCard from '@components/ui/FeatureCard.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Voxivium — A Public Benefit Corporation for civic accountability"
  description="Voxivium is a Public Benefit Corporation building a non-partisan platform for political accountability and transparency. Read about our mission and internal commitments."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About Voxivium</p>
      <h1>A government of the people, by the people, for the people...</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Voxivium exists to repair the broken connection between citizens and the people elected to
        serve them. We're a Public Benefit Corporation building a non-partisan platform for
        political accountability, transparency, and informed civic engagement.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mission">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Our mission</p>
      <h2>Close the gap between what constituents want and what their representatives do.</h2>
      <p>
        Voters feel unheard — worn down by a media diet of outrage and a political class that seems
        to answer first to donors and primary extremists. Politicians, even well-intentioned ones,
        govern from incomplete signals: short polls, the loudest inbox, and the assumption that the
        party platform reflects the district. Both sides are working in the dark.
      </p>
      <p>
        Voxivium turns the lights on with a single, honest measurement: how often does your
        representative vote the way you'd vote? When the verified positions of millions of voters
        are aggregated and weighted by what they care about, voters discover they aren't alone,
        and politicians get a mandate they can actually govern by. Most Americans agree on more than
        they think. We're building the data layer that lets them prove it.
      </p>
      <p>
        This isn't a marketing line. It's encoded in our corporate charter, which legally requires
        us to balance financial returns with public benefit. Success has to be measured both in
        revenue and in outcomes for democracy.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="why-pbc">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Why a Public Benefit Corporation?</h2>
      <p>
        A traditional C-corp has one duty: maximize shareholder value. That duty conflicts—often
        quietly, sometimes loudly—with the public interest a civic platform needs to serve. As a
        Public Benefit Corporation, our directors have a legal obligation to consider the impact of
        decisions on the citizens we serve, not only on shareholders.
      </p>
      <p>
        We chose this structure because the work demands it. A platform built to hold power
        accountable cannot answer first to investors who want growth at any cost. Voxivium answers
        first to the people whose voices it carries.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="commitments">
    <div class="container">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">Internal commitments</p>
        <h2>What we hold ourselves to.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          To demand better government, we hold ourselves to a higher standard of corporate
          governance. These commitments are codified in our bylaws.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="grid">
        <FeatureCard title="5:1 pay ratio">
          <p>
            Total compensation between our highest-paid executive and our lowest-paid employee is
            capped at 5:1. The number is in our bylaws, not just our values deck.
          </p>
        </FeatureCard>

        <FeatureCard title="Living wage">
          <p>
            Every Voxivium employee, contractor, and intern earns a locality-adjusted living wage—no
            exceptions, no roles excluded.
          </p>
        </FeatureCard>

        <FeatureCard title="Profit sharing">
          <p>
            After necessary operational reserves, profits are shared with employees. The people
            building the platform share in its upside.
          </p>
        </FeatureCard>

        <FeatureCard title="Privacy by design">
          <p>
            Individual user data is never for sale. Every paid product is built on aggregated,
            anonymized signal—and the bylaws bind us to keep it that way.
          </p>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: clamp(4rem, 10vh, 6rem) 1.5rem 2rem;
  }

  .container {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--color-brand-primary);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.875rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-brand-text1);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.15;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.5vw, 1.875rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-brand-text1);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .page-hero .lead {
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    color: var(--color-brand-text2);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 36rem;
  }

  .mission,
  .why-pbc {
    padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .mission p,
  .why-pbc p {
    color: var(--color-brand-text2);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }

  .mission p:last-child,
  .why-pbc p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .commitments {
    padding: clamp(3rem, 8vh, 5rem) 1.5rem;
    background: var(--color-brand-surface);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--color-brand-el1);
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .commitments .container {
    max-width: 64rem;
  }

  .commitments header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .commitments .lead {
    margin: 1rem auto 0;
    color: var(--color-brand-text3);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
